{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "canvas-operation-pipeline",
  "title": "How one canvas edit call runs",
  "description": "Pipeline that every Codecaine Canvas edit tool runs, from tool definition to result (canvas/src/session/tools/operations/operation-tool.ts).\n\n**Reading order**: top row left to right: Tool definition (OperationSpec → defineOperationTool → Tool descriptor), then Runtime validation (Schema validation, with its own runtime validation error end). The `execute` wire enters runOperation, whose 13 stages run top to bottom in four columns, left to right: Run the edit (1–3), Reconcile the draft (4–6), Guard checks (7–10), Commit and report (11–13). Each stage links to the next with `next`. The four guard checks are decision diamonds phrased as the question that fails the call: heldMoves (held object would move?), zero delta (board already matches?), newBrokenWires (self-loop, dangling or zero-length wire?) and the section rule (section pairs before/after refused?). Stage details sit in node names and one short note per column; the known waypoint-replay gap sits in the Commit and report note.\n\n**Results** (bottom row, Call results): ERROR takes one entry per meaning: `any error` from spec.validate (left), `growing would pull a neighbor in` from Section auto-grow (top), and the unlabelled fail exits of the three guard diamonds as one trunk (right). NO-OP takes `yes` from the zero-delta check (top) and `status noop` from spec.apply (left). The green `APPLIED headline` wire runs from operationPerception to APPLIED. ERROR and NO-OP both lead to \"Draft unchanged, no event\"; an edge-target NO-OP also carries the edge's numbered route. Only the commit column changes the board. Result node names carry the result line formats.\n\n**Color key**: blue nodes = tool definition; violet = pipeline stage; orange diamonds = checks; green = commit path / APPLIED; red = error; gray = no-op / unchanged.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
